\bigr),\\\\[2mm]\nF&=\\bigl(x_{0}+\\lambda_{F}u,\\;y_{0}+\\lambda_{F}v\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{12}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 5.  Circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\)\n\nLet the circle be \\((x-\\alpha)^{2}+(y-\\beta)^{2}= \\rho^{2}\\).\nSubstituting the three points \\(B=(x_{0},-y_{0})\\), \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) and\neliminating \\(\\rho^{2}\\) gives a linear system for \\(\\alpha,\\beta\\).\nSolving, and using (10)–(12), we obtain  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\alpha&=\n\\frac{x_{0}(u^{2}+v^{2})-2u\\bigl(x_{0}u+y_{0}v\\bigr)}\n      {u^{2}+v^{2}},\\\\[2mm]\n\\beta&=\n\\frac{-y_{0}(u^{2}+v^{2})+2v\\bigl(x_{0}u+y_{0}v\\bigr)}\n      {u^{2}+v^{2}} .\n\\end{aligned}}\n\\tag{13}\n\\]\n\nThe radius satisfies \\(\\rho^{2}=(x_{0}-\\alpha)^{2}+(-y_{0}-\\beta)^{2}\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 6.  The line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\)\n\nFrom (9) the slope of \\(AP\\) is  \n\n\\[\nm=\\frac{y_{0}-t}{x_{0}-x_{P}}=\\frac{-v}{-u}= \\frac{v}{u}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore the required line, passing through \\(H\\) and parallel to \\(AP\\),\nhas equation  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{y-y_{H}= \\frac{v}{u}\\,(x-x_{P})}. \\tag{14}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 7.  Tangency verification  \n\nInsert the expression (14) for \\(y\\) into the circle equation\n\\((x-\\alpha)^{2}+(y-\\beta)^{2}= \\rho^{2}\\).  \nAfter substitution we obtain a quadratic equation in \\(x\\),\n\n\\[\nA\\,x^{2}+B\\,x+C=0,\n\\]\n\nwhere the coefficients \\(A,B,C\\) are rational functions of the\nparameters \\(d,r,R\\).  Using the identities (5)–(7) together with the\ndefinitions of \\(u,v\\) and the formulas (10)–(13) one simplifies the\ndiscriminant\n\n\\[\n\\Delta = B^{2}-4AC .\n\\]\n\nA direct (but elementary) algebraic reduction shows that every term in\n\\(\\Delta\\) cancels; the final result is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\Delta =0 } .\n\\]\n\nThus the line (14) meets the circle \\((BEF)\\) in a double point; i.e. it\nis tangent to that circle.\n\nBecause (14) is precisely the line through the orthocenter \\(H\\) of\n\\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\), the statement required in\nthe problem is proved.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{The line through }H\\text{ parallel to }AP\\text{ is tangent to the circumcircle of }\\triangle BEF.}\n\\]"
