he circle having centre \\(P\\)) to the circle\n\\((BEF)\\) (the circle having centre \\(O\\)).  Hence  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal S(P)=O . \\tag{2}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 2.  The position of \\(O\\)\n\nSince \\(\\mathcal S\\) is centred at \\(A\\), the image of any point lies on\nthe ray issued from \\(A\\) through that point; therefore from (2)\n\n\\[\nO\\in AP . \\tag{3}\n\\]\n\nFrom (1) we see that \\(\\mathcal S\\) sends the line \\(MN\\) onto itself,\nhence the image of any point of \\(MN\\) again belongs to \\(MN\\).  In\nparticular, the image of \\(P\\) (which is \\(O\\)) lies on \\(MN\\); thus\n\n\\[\nO\\in MN . \\tag{4}\n\\]\n\nConsequently  \n\n\\[\nO=AP\\cap MN . \\tag{5}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 3.  Perpendicularity of \\(AP\\) to the common chord \\(AB\\)\n\nThe common chord \\(AB\\) of the two intersecting circles is orthogonal to\nthe line joining their centres; therefore  \n\n\\[\nAB\\perp MN . \\tag{6}\n\\]\n\nFrom (5) we have \\(AO\\subseteq MN\\); together with (6) this yields  \n\n\\[\nAO\\perp AB . \\tag{7}\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(O\\) lies on \\(AP\\), (7) gives  \n\n\\[\nAP\\perp AB . \\tag{8}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 4.  The orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\)\n\nIn \\(\\triangle PMN\\) the altitude from the vertex \\(P\\) is the line\nthrough \\(P\\) perpendicular to the opposite side \\(MN\\); its foot is the\northocentre \\(H\\).  Hence  \n\n\\[\nPH\\perp MN . \\tag{9}\n\\]\n\nCombining (6) and (9) we obtain  \n\n\\[\nPH\\parallel AB . \\tag{10}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5.  The tangent line\n\nLet \\(\\ell\\) be the line through \\(H\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\).\nFrom (8) we have \\(AP\\perp AB\\); using (10) we deduce  \n\n\\[\n\\ell\\perp AB\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \\ell\\perp AO .\n\\]\n\nSince \\(O\\) is the centre of the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\), the\nradius \\(AO\\) is perpendicular to the tangent at the point where the\ntangent meets the circle.  Therefore the line \\(\\ell\\), which passes\nthrough \\(H\\) and is perpendicular to \\(AO\\), is tangent to the\ncircumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\nThus the line through the orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is\nparallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\). \u220e"
